  "decisions": [
    "Retain scoped EDIT state facade instead of private USER receive shell. BEGINRECV_HWND resolves an enrolled borrowed window; caller owns task/runtime scope. Original EnterCrit/LeaveCrit cannot manipulate modern USER private state. Keep signature and local FNID algorithm.",
    "Original NtUserSetWindowFNID body is exact. Facade initializes retval to FALSE whereas original macro leaves it uninitialized when FNID already set. Fixture asserts rejection for repeated EDIT and changed BUTTON and permits repeated CLEANEDUP. Retain deterministic rejection; do not call modern native FNID on retained old WND.",
    "StubExceptionHandler has no retained call in this subset. Remove unused macro and its orphan diagnostic frame together when reconciling original subset structure; this is partial cleanup, not whole-file deletion.",
    "DATAALIGN/CHARALIGN are defined and undefined around no retained class-registration body. Remove these unused macros and associated detached alignment frame with coherent subset reconciliation.",
    "Detached NEVER, FE_IME, DEBUG/DBG, MEMPHIS and x86 alignment frames survive outside omitted functions, often with empty selected bodies. Reconstruct source-policy-compliant retained subset structure from original owner ranges; do not activate omitted private server code. Preserve logical line 6170 for the retained function.",
    "Omitted receive stubs cover desktop/window-station, messages, menus, clipboard, controls, input, painting, WOW cleanup and thread state. Private probes/locks are not composable wholesale; classify reached client edges against existing original client/native bindings before asserting every omitted wrapper policy is redundant. Definition inventory is evidence indexing, not body equivalence.",
    "Omitted post-FNID wrappers include style/thread state, window creation, class registration, properties, keyboard and scrollbar policy. Compare reached original client callers and current bounded providers, including structure conversion and failure semantics; native API availability alone is insufficient.",
    "Omitted MESSAGECALL and hook marshalling use private window locks, probing and CALLPROC. Compare selected original message converters, actual callback ownership and exceptional copyback before accepting whole omission; do not copy NT4 syscall numbers or create a second dispatcher.",
    "Input-language acceptance and media-change notification omitted. Separate guest-visible charset/keyboard policy from host-system event ownership; establish selected caller coverage before deciding restore or retain omission."
  ],
